<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex -sĕco</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exĕco</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exĭco</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 34</span></i>), cŭi,
		ctum, 1 (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.
				subj.</i> exsecaveris, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			42</span></i>), v. a., <i>to cut out</i> or <i>away.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitiosas partes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 1, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pestem aliquam tamquam strumam civitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Sest. 65, 135</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linguam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Clu. 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornu (frontis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 5, 59</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">varices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 78 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fetum ventri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 55, 81, § 217</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventrem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					28, 2, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filium alicui mortuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 50, 16, 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nervos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 2, 33, 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundum armarii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Clu. 64, 179</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			partic., <i>to cut</i>, <i>castrate</i>,
				<i>geld</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetus haec opinio Graeciam opplevit exsectum
					Caelum a filio Saturno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 2, 24, 63</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 6, 2,
				2</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and in a Greek construction: infelix ferro
					mollita juventus Atque exsecta virum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					10, 134</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsectus et exemptus honoribus senatoriis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 2, 12, 3</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b>, of interest: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quinas hic capiti mercedes exsecat (=extorquet,
					extundit),</span>”
				<i>cuts out</i>, <i>deducts</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 2, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
